<title>MEXICO: Bank of Mexico completes money market operation.</title>
<headline>Bank of Mexico completes money market operation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Mexico completed its operation to drain 1.594 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday via three direct sales and three repurchasing agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The terms of the three direct sales were as follows:</p>
<p>		   AMOUNT	   TERM	   RATE (PERCENT)</p>
<p>		   150 million	 342 days	21.65</p>
<p>		   150 million	 180 days	21.50</p>
<p>		   150 million	  90 days	21.28</p>
<p>The terms for the three repurchase agreements were as follows:</p>
<p>		   AMOUNT	   TERM	   RATE (PERCENT)</p>
<p>		   400 million	 34 days	 22.95</p>
<p>		   500 million	 25 days	 23.00</p>
<p>		   244 million	  3 days	 23.78</p>
<p>((--Caroline Brothers, Mexico City newsroom +252 729 7902))</p>
